{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/241996-modern-sidereal-larceny-and-lack-of-wyld-presence","id":241996,"title":"[Modern]Sidereal Larceny and Lack of Wyld Presence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-26T22:28:29-07:00","id":241996,"title":"[Modern]Sidereal Larceny and Lack of Wyld Presence","content":"This is a pretty simple topic, and yet I haven't really found an answer of my own. I'm currently playing a Chosen of Secrets in a Modern game. My character is invested in Sidereal Larceny, but his development of this ability has stalled. The reason is simple: the capstone that the Larceny Charmset builds up to, Conning Chaos Technique, just... falls flat for me in a Modern setting. Don't get me wrong; the power of cursing someone with the attention of Chaos and its fae hordes still <i>works </i>- mechanically and narratively - but it just doesn't really have the same impact, the same 'meaningfulness,' so to speak, when the Wyld is a distant concern and chaos isn't actually gnawing at the edges of your world. And, of course, the part about Wyld-tainted areas being returned to normalcy just... doesn't really work. Trading someone's life against respite for a Wyld-plagued land doesn't mean much when the raksha are weirdo aliens from space rather than the endless armies of the storm at the end of the world.<br /> <br /> So, basically. Does anyone have suggestions for replacing the Sidereal Larceny capstone in Modern with something more impactful, or failing that for tweaking it into something more suitable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T07:59:54-07:00","id":242252,"title":"","content":"I've always felt the important bit of that charm was the curse -- so make that the forefront of the charm. Like, you steal someone's very luck, dooming them to ill fortune until you use the stolen luck to get automatic success on a roll or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T01:07:44-07:00","id":242896,"title":"","content":"I take it that this isn't The Modern Age?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T09:26:13-07:00","id":245385,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's break this down:<br /> <br /> 1) Corebook says that Larceny covers &quot;legerdemain, sleight of hand, gambling, pickpocketing, disguise, lock picking, con games and similar skills...also includes knowledge of the habits and customs of the criminal underworld.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Sidereal charms are sometimes direct, but are often indirect and work through inversion, or approach their Ability from odd angles. Sidereal Larceny, in particular, largely focuses on stealing intangibles, such as dreams, names, and trains-of-thought. I looked up the Secrets Resplendencies, but none of them really seem oriented to Larceny, the closest was The Mask, and it's pretty clearly Stealth.<br /> <br /> 3) Sidereal capstone charms are usually Ability 5, Ess 4, and are broadly powerful in a story-enhancing way, almost like Fairy Tale spells. They often involve prayer strips that morph into some symbolic form during the charms' duration. <br /> <br /> Run it all together and what do you get?<br /> <br /> I'm honestly not sure, there are a lot of possibilities. The first that comes to mind is complete Identity Theft, similar to the Stealth capstone, Ceasing to Exist Approach, only it allows you to steal a particular target's appearance, identity and Destiny (either giving them Arcane Fate or one of your Resplendent Destinies). A similar idea is one that temporarily makes you into the shadowy Kingpin of local organized crime; everyone suddenly recognizes you as the &quot;Overboss&quot; that they just remembered existed, and fall all over themselves to please you (giving you temporary access to expanded Backgrounds). <br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm not thinking &quot;weird and indirect&quot; enough. Any other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T11:58:43-07:00","id":245526,"title":"","content":"Sidereal Charms, even the capstones (which are always prayer strip Charms) are not always broadly powerful story-enhancing fairy tale effects, nor are they necessarily weird and indirect. Look at Harmonic Completion. Sure it has a <i>mythic</i> style to it, with the blindfold, but otherwise? It's &quot;make your Performance rolls awesome, tack on UMI which makes further social attacks easier and make targets' perpetuating your ideas better; and do it for five days.&quot; Look at Implicit Construction Methodology. It's &quot;fate builds stuff for me.&quot; For a tree all about fate-crafting, it's pretty straightforward. Wilderness Commanding Practice is basically previous Survival Charms stacked together and souped up. Wanting and Fearing Prayer is &quot;fabricate a relationship between two people&quot; which is a straightforward extension of the whole tree's messing with peoples' relationships. Invisible Motion is basically an extension of Inexorable Advance, which both straightforward applications of Athletic's theme of &quot;economy of motion&quot;. It's effect is also just a blatant teleport. Perfection of the Visionary Warrior is a scattering of buffs and a free one attack flurry with any weapon. Which again is a straightforward extension of Melee's multiple-combat-Abilities theme.<br /> <br /> That all said, there <i>are</i> a lot of broadly applicable story-enhancing fairy tale effects as the prayer strip Charms, but a good portion of them are not.<br /> <br /> Alright now let's take a closer look Sidereal Larceny. My interpretation of its theme is &quot;Theft of abstract things.&quot; I'll reiterate what I said in a post long ago on the subject:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love this theme. It's so very direct, as it's still taking things, still theft, but of anything but normal physical objects. Very mystical, and we end up with a lot of fun Charms (though sadly many fall flat).<br /> <br /> Thought-Swiping Distraction steals thoughts. Sidereal Shell Games steal dice out of pools. Name-Pilfering Practice steals names. Dream-Confiscation steals dreams. Avoiding the Truth Technique doesn't really fit \u2014 and for good reason. It used to be a Lore Charm in 1e, and its theme (&quot;secrets that are best left hidden / horrible truths&quot;) still applies here. Nor does Masque of the Uncanny, really, since you just adopt a disguise of something outside of Creation. (This is probably because it was one of the new Charms added in 2e. It could've fit the theme much better if it was about stealing someone's or something's image.) Conning Chaos Technique is a blown-up version of the theme (as nearly all prayer strip Charms are) being a con instead of a theft, and with destiny and the Wyld as its abstracts. </div> </div> </div>As a prayer strip Charm, it should be a blown up version of the Ability's theme, either in a straightforward manner (as I explained above) or in a much less direct manner like many of the other Sidereal prayer strip Charms. Conning Chaos was much more one of those less direction extensions of the themes, as it wasn't a straight-up theft of something, but a con that produces new land in Creation and curses someone with bad luck.<br /> <br /> So, for something more impactful, I'll reiterate my first post in having it be a theft of someone's luck is good and relatively straightforward which doesn't require much work. Just cut out the Wyld reclamation effect and replace the current curse effect (Fair Folk taking a liking to you, possible mutations) with general bad luck. Like Eclipse Cast botch effects, raised target numbers on rolls, or even simply generally increased difficulties and more disastrous results on failed rolls. Leave in the ability for the victim to make rolls to understand their curse, so they're not completely fucked.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, Hand-of-Omega's full-on identity theft is not bad either, and is probably even more useful in Modern. For something somewhat more narrative, an expensive theft of <i>any</i> abstract would be a fun Charm, though obviously very reliant on ST adjudication (so it depends on if you/your ST likes that kind of thing or not.) Something slightly more specific would be theft on an <i>idea</i>. Like Name-Pilfering Practice but much more powerful -- making it so nobody can recall the idea. That, I think, fits Modern well, as it plays into the conspiratorial overtones of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}